375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (documentation on the EwE suite and its modelling framework. Primary sources include an EwE suite user's guide \(Christensen et al., 2023\) that includes modelling tutorials and examples of how to obtain data, and a published textbook designed for explaining concepts and teaching a course on Ecopath with Ecosim \(Christensen & Walters, 2024\), which includes background information and explanations of the underlying framework. Both of these textbooks are freely available online and under a Creative Commons license to incentivise collaboration, including for commercial purposes. The tutorials and information presented in both of these textbooks are not directly transferable to Rpath and require a bridging of information based on the differences in inputs and user interface. To aid in this bridging, Rpath, like all packages in R, contains information on its functions and a series of vignettes that demonstrate the core functionality of the package, however the vignettes are by no means a replacement for dedicated tutorials and documentation that act as a user guide for Rpath or aiding in the transition between Rpath and EwE. It is also worth noting that the Rpath vignettes are not tutorials on the EwE modelling framework within Rpath; they are demonstrations of how to build and run the model, described on the basis that the user has an understanding of what they are doing and why they would be doing it. At the time of )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
